cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LUMOS in research, cite the software and the associated paper or preprint when available."
title: "LUMOS: Localized Unified Monitoring Optimization System"
type: software
version: 3.1.1
date-released: 2026-07-26
license: MIT
abstract: "A stable public socially constrained sequential Bayesian framework and browser-based tool for Heat, Air, Soil, and Water monitoring design, validation, intervention evaluation, cross-domain funding, robust multi-round policy analysis, verified deployment, field campaigns, live outcome tracking, commissioning, calibration, maintenance, and replacement planning."
keywords:
  - environmental monitoring
  - Bayesian experimental design
  - sensor placement
  - environmental justice
  - robust optimization
  - adaptive monitoring
  - heat risk
  - air quality
  - soil health
  - water quality
